From: =?UTF-8?q?Bedirhan=20Gen=C3=A7aslan?=
 <b2210356065@cs.hacettepe.edu.tr>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 20:49:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 04/71] Scope reasoning to the turn that produced it

The client used to strip every reasoning item out of the request, so the
model lost its own plan the moment it made a tool call and had to rederive
it on each step of the agentic loop.

Reasoning items now carry the id of the turn that produced them, and the
context manager keeps them only while that turn is still running. Once the
turn ends they drop out of every later prompt, so the cache cost is bounded
to one turn body per turn boundary instead of growing without limit. The
compaction paths pass no active turn, so they still see no reasoning at all.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
